#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115153 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115321 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdaed02f-09f2-5572-a70c-0e6979ef2167" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For the Union of Two Opposite-Sided Linear Inequalities that Overlap"}] :question/id #uuid "abae2e99-53b7-5d81-860c-9555ce50ec3a" :question/math-academy-id "e-965" :question/problem "Find all the values of $x$ that satisfy $12x+8 > 44$ or $5x+3 \\leq 28.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by solving $12x+8 > 44\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12x+8 & >44 \\\\ 12x & >36 \\\\ x & >3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/e9/e9eec85ca2dd2a9fd01db97a5f281d16fd958e143e048f7ff3c5e7a87dd33f0a.png)\n\nThen, we solve $5x+3 \\leq 28\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+3 & \\le 28 \\\\ 5x & \\le 25 \\\\ x & \\le 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/c9/c9cec5cfc0e476fffe4f89f89ff0585992855e8e36fe09778029d5accd2bdc6b.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/dd/dd1330c9f2d9dc2140a3e3a4dc37ac269d134c5e367f59c9985ce04d4acd6304.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $-\\infty < x < \\infty.$ We can write this using interval notation as $(-\\infty,\\infty).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115154 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115322 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91a5169c-6a92-535d-85e1-8b9363b49274" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Union of Two Linear Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "81405a9f-882c-50fb-8057-41bb54515d14" :question/math-academy-id "e-966" :question/problem "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $6x-1 \\leq 2$ or $5x-1 > 9.$ Express your answer in interval notation." :question/worked-solution "We start by solving $6x-1 \\leq 2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-1 & \\le 2 \\\\ 6x & \\le 3 \\\\ x & \\le \\frac{3}{6} \\\\ x & \\le \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/dd/dd2c101e02e14a147371bc1b822f3bc86081dd0059ac50ae1f9131909e73e3ad.png)\n\nThen, we solve $5x -1 > 9\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-1 & >9 \\\\ 5x & >10 \\\\ x & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/8b/8b252e1c42dcac87072a33b33460a887b6ec3bfa0d1511f05a004935df1911ca.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/ac/ac44f335b135463820ec0db9bc04470769fee7aabc8717edcc351893b6d8de47.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $x \\leq \\dfrac{1}{2}$ or $x >2.$ We can write this using interval notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-\\infty ,\\frac{1}{2}]\\cup (2,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115155 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115323 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e3a4ead-02d0-5023-a7a7-3aaaca19b563" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Union of Two Linear Inequalities When One Inequality is Compound"}] :question/id #uuid "dced871e-e24d-5d06-a4bb-9faa933ecac7" :question/math-academy-id "e-967" :question/problem "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $1 < 5x+6 \\leq 11$ or $5x-7 > 8.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by solving $1 < 5x+6 \\leq 11\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & <5x+6\\le 11 \\\\ -5 & <5x\\le 5 \\\\ -1 & <x\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/69/69948e87bc893a2461ec6e8bb77dd72e77e6d496970e31df899400c42238cd01.png)\n\nThen, we solve $5x-7 > 8\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-7 & >8 \\\\ 5x & >15 \\\\ x & >3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/10/10bb9a3bcc0b13b015649e2dae70a3ff3dcd361f46e6c545182031d6e095ad16.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/84/84a05cd47818c9609609c2f02bd026ccadfa77c6641dff82936630bf04fbe77e.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $-1 <  x \\leq 1$ or $x > 3.$ We can write this using interval notation as\n\n$$\n(-1,1] \\cup (3,\\infty).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115576 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115323 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e3a4ead-02d0-5023-a7a7-3aaaca19b563" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Union of Two Linear Inequalities When One Inequality is Compound"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d137874c-bb8c-5162-b65c-db2434d9f972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bc/bc365364192f3784c565ebcb819a5f37885830f93510029647d39883217987cb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112435} {:answer/id #uuid "098e7fff-d314-54e3-bf48-76ed174495f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/56/56134a3d0faa3bc166e13b274a85860d112c1205e474a5bb932f2d15878a6772.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112436} {:answer/id #uuid "0afcbfd5-6834-5558-9832-342f694fe757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1a/1ad54d12cf04e7142b0bcdd78484d9098fd9ca689f464fc5c03f1dbb0671569f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112437} {:answer/id #uuid "107e0e50-1e2a-5e90-a4e9-30472ac651e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b1/b18806e4132590b3ac68afdae1f13b52e0b16365eabc1445fab2ba73c38ac469.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112438} {:answer/id #uuid "25fdf11c-2ca5-5538-a199-e11b6f644330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/64/64975857d503b11711a025e5bb8c16ad7c8a877db061ebc0cbdb59189ed9d9f7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d137874c-bb8c-5162-b65c-db2434d9f972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bc/bc365364192f3784c565ebcb819a5f37885830f93510029647d39883217987cb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112435} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4041cc0-0ef3-5283-b5d3-550930e80759" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112434}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "710e74cf-0030-5cf8-afcc-101ba583257c" :question/math-academy-id "q-25484" :question/problem "What is the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $2\\le 2x+6\\le 10$ or $8x+7\\le -9?$" :question/worked-solution "We start by solving $2\\le 2x+6\\le 10:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & \\le 2x+6\\le 10 \\\\ -4 & \\le 2x\\le 4 \\\\ -2 & \\le x\\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/1a/1ad54d12cf04e7142b0bcdd78484d9098fd9ca689f464fc5c03f1dbb0671569f.png)\n\nThen, we solve $8x+7\\le -9:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x+7 & \\le -9 \\\\ 8x & \\le -16 \\\\ x & \\le -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/12/12c34a5af230afb788ddd8c689ef0e9b29c5c5adaf35a1e81099453436cf7f3f.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/bc/bc365364192f3784c565ebcb819a5f37885830f93510029647d39883217987cb.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $x\\le 2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115323 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e3a4ead-02d0-5023-a7a7-3aaaca19b563" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Union of Two Linear Inequalities When One Inequality is Compound"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d0acf1f-a695-5686-a3d8-ca71b52cb1a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{4}{5})\\cup (\\frac{7}{2},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509747} {:answer/id #uuid "6edda186-30b5-5a11-8092-91ddd1baad9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{4}{5})\\cup (\\frac{4}{5},\\frac{7}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509915} {:answer/id #uuid "7a942b8e-874e-5ef9-8924-ccec67882267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{4}{5})\\cup (\\frac{7}{2},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509949} {:answer/id #uuid "9ef9de4b-be83-5f15-bc32-f9912d585882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{7}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510020} {:answer/id #uuid "ca402586-983d-5d04-8c66-0efb1ad988e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d0acf1f-a695-5686-a3d8-ca71b52cb1a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{4}{5})\\cup (\\frac{7}{2},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509747} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbac6049-90c6-5602-a97a-d27179f99520" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d1dc12b-037c-55bd-92e4-67849dd74463" :question/math-academy-id "q-25489" :question/problem "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $4x-5>9$ or $3<10x+8<16.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by solving $4x-5>9:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-5 & >9 \\\\ 4x & >14 \\\\ x & >\\frac{14}{4} \\\\ x & >\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/e3/e39459442837c3de83da860526c5f39b048d02b33b6ea0a3340efd599bb880d3.png)\n\nThen, we solve $3<10x+8<16:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & <10x+8<16 \\\\ 3-8 & <10x<16-8 \\\\ -5 & <10x<8 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{10} & <x<\\frac{8}{10} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & <x<\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/61/611944fd64cf3638f0cfd4ae8f8a658496af927adc7b91f68e7aafdd36817272.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/11/112f50397f85c79e51650d88d2d4125cdb5479e60af579836bc3c8cd4eb22276.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $x>\\frac{7}{2}$ or $-\\frac{1}{2}<x<\\frac{4}{5}.$ We can write this using interval notation as\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{4}{5})\\cup (\\frac{7}{2},\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510386 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115321 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdaed02f-09f2-5572-a70c-0e6979ef2167" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For the Union of Two Opposite-Sided Linear Inequalities that Overlap"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18a48c20-6697-5de3-bfb1-aa373a9d1cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/31/312b09109c1cb34d5820616c9aca887c6e48507be2c5045b128f9fa8c4cb0791.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509735} {:answer/id #uuid "3f0bb42e-c190-5229-bb2a-774c46c2ed0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/66/6681d256a848077367d83e215b4cb45edea86c49929c9c85c2aa32d8caaa2de7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509822} {:answer/id #uuid "971a3595-9f9d-5d9b-ba15-4f12ff874cf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b2/b2b7aad327466abf2472e9058317e8f5521eba35a944482e2cc3cc12cf51095b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510005} {:answer/id #uuid "c3cf020d-1363-526d-838a-54966d7c8d0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0b/0b9f413bd97b2b411b8a134441e6a6fdad5052df71ba33c33280f2c6850eb7ae.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510099} {:answer/id #uuid "fa38eaa9-fde9-5ac1-8936-620024312893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No real solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f0bb42e-c190-5229-bb2a-774c46c2ed0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/66/6681d256a848077367d83e215b4cb45edea86c49929c9c85c2aa32d8caaa2de7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509822} :answer-field/id #uuid "41293c54-1759-5e11-8b8c-9e3094059bbe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510272}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4351a80f-5497-5bde-b1ce-3fcb89da7609" :question/math-academy-id "q-25591" :question/problem "Which of the following number lines represents the values of $x$ that satisfy $7x+5>47$ or $3x-3\\le 30?$" :question/worked-solution "We start by solving $7x+5>47:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+5 & >47 \\\\ 7x & >47-5 \\\\ 7x & >42 \\\\ x & >\\frac{42}{7} \\\\ x & >6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/b2/b2b7aad327466abf2472e9058317e8f5521eba35a944482e2cc3cc12cf51095b.png)\n\nThen, we solve $3x-3\\le 30:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-3 & \\le 30 \\\\ 3x & \\le 30+3 \\\\ 3x & \\le 33 \\\\ x & \\le \\frac{33}{3} \\\\ x & \\le 11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/31/312b09109c1cb34d5820616c9aca887c6e48507be2c5045b128f9fa8c4cb0791.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/66/6681d256a848077367d83e215b4cb45edea86c49929c9c85c2aa32d8caaa2de7.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $-\\infty <x<\\infty .$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510428 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115322 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91a5169c-6a92-535d-85e1-8b9363b49274" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Union of Two Linear Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1222ea73-7e26-5f9b-93f4-9aa59eaf76cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509720} {:answer/id #uuid "7353cd84-2e2e-5e4a-96d3-14bfcec424f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,2]\\cup (3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509928} {:answer/id #uuid "938f28b1-c360-5ccd-b701-56e4b8b4fd3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,2)\\cup [3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509999} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a86e05-1a21-59c0-84ef-df8a50afc8e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510036} {:answer/id #uuid "c8a9a619-1500-5c95-b104-a810b516b82f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7353cd84-2e2e-5e4a-96d3-14bfcec424f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,2]\\cup (3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509928} :answer-field/id #uuid "66fe9ad0-b164-5fc3-a63f-e6ebefcc66a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510294}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9ea10a00-dd11-5690-aa60-169c6a36b74a" :question/math-academy-id "q-28961" :question/problem "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $3x+5>14$ or $2x-3\\le 1.$ Express your answer in interval notation." :question/worked-solution "We start by solving $3x+5>14:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+5 & >14 \\\\ 3x & >9 \\\\ x & >3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/5d/5dca213f8266a9bd001380b30368e5996b24fa2ddb6d3aef5670befde451e77d.png)\n\nThen, we solve $2x-3\\le 1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3 & \\le 1 \\\\ 2x & \\le 4 \\\\ x & \\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/45/454e1de1e32bb5e3fb03dc280076414493d9e4a9c042246be565d8550c2012f2.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/53/531c59b67623a10db6af4236187e7d50315e7068585d6a5e6882db0d1997bdce.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $x\\le 2$ or $x>3.$ We can write this using interval notation as\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,2]\\cup (3,\\infty ).\\,\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510418 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115323 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e3a4ead-02d0-5023-a7a7-3aaaca19b563" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Union of Two Linear Inequalities When One Inequality is Compound"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dc360a4-3724-5f32-8d03-0c02d7c587f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{4},0)\\cup [\\frac{7}{4},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509913} {:answer/id #uuid "7195a570-e270-5793-802f-906d24f44063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{4},\\frac{3}{2})\\cup [\\frac{7}{4},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509923} {:answer/id #uuid "a825b680-9363-5985-8b72-a7133059db3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{7}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510045} {:answer/id #uuid "b17e291b-b445-5794-8977-135119a3a0ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{4},0)\\cup [\\frac{1}{4},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510071} {:answer/id #uuid "e3f18e78-6255-505a-b02a-60b50e82717b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[2,3)\\cup [4,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7195a570-e270-5793-802f-906d24f44063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{4},\\frac{3}{2})\\cup [\\frac{7}{4},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509923} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dd10fbd-61f3-54a4-a711-5930036f3a9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510269}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "83a6d940-fad6-59a8-acb5-f275a8b09b93" :question/math-academy-id "q-28988" :question/problem "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $2<4x-3<3$ or $4x-3\\ge 4.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by solving $2<4x-3<3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & <4x-3<3 \\\\ 5 & <4x<6 \\\\ \\frac{5}{4} & <x<\\frac{6}{4} \\\\ \\frac{5}{4} & <x<\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/ba/bac195a89ad5d09fa7753fe32bc5f4633453d37816c53330321e000579a8cb85.png)\n\nThen, we solve $4x-3\\ge 4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3 & \\ge 4 \\\\ 4x & \\ge 7 \\\\ x & \\ge \\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/09/09fd2be8420b15d39149183d5b802fdcdbd20739ab7364663e0592e61aaf12df.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/6a/6ac5a412c535841b9872b1cbe4edee815e173dd43f3bb757616b7ca9a68200b8.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $\\frac{5}{4}<x<\\frac{3}{2}$ or $x\\ge \\frac{7}{4}.$ We can write this using interval notation as\n\n$$\n(\\frac{5}{4},\\frac{3}{2})\\cup [\\frac{7}{4},\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115322 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91a5169c-6a92-535d-85e1-8b9363b49274" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Union of Two Linear Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69cbea69-6868-5ccb-858f-b44009caa759" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,2)\\cup [3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509907} {:answer/id #uuid "6c0a897f-4ef6-57d6-9980-9e293186af3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,2]\\cup (5,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509911} {:answer/id #uuid "9e778703-e474-5e5f-a85c-446ac10186dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[2,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510017} {:answer/id #uuid "dbd7961f-1cd9-5059-bc70-26ad3c31e036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,25]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510156} {:answer/id #uuid "f488b71a-7a5a-591e-aefc-dfc045886d0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup [-1,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c0a897f-4ef6-57d6-9980-9e293186af3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,2]\\cup (5,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509911} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a64adf4-89bb-5bcd-a5d3-aeb6554ac2a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89c9046d-3e0b-5226-98f7-31a9c44e0e5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-51768" :question/problem "Find the set of values of $w$ that satisfy $w-3\\le -1$ or $5w>25.$ Express your answer in interval notation." :question/worked-solution "We start by solving $w-3\\le -1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-3+3 & \\le -1+3 \\\\ w & \\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/41/41894afbf397505568367e80d14e34fe2b04a2acdfd5398bd8ba41727b8c67c6.png)\n\nThen, we solve $5w>25:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5w}{5} & >\\frac{25}{5} \\\\ w & >5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/26/262a3e683cb8c8a67cdd58c0f138e44466c346092c7f74ec03ec1483a385056a.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $w$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/95/95d67331522c16093207de451a33bb713b42e1418d1f4c1a7aa1ef6369a51e4b.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $w\\le 2$ or $w>5.$ We can write this using interval notation as\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,2]\\cup (5,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115903 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115321 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdaed02f-09f2-5572-a70c-0e6979ef2167" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For the Union of Two Opposite-Sided Linear Inequalities that Overlap"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c1f2322-151c-5711-b590-478752f7aac8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c9/c9f85fc4864f321722a7cb0b017eab1979aa6a84cd07d08b150b625a1720f25a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114356} {:answer/id #uuid "ec152d47-a4ec-5e78-905c-db1d5493f9c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2a/2ae1ee1d90025b9c2c3adce0d55055540aed2aa866a2a708cf6533cd06e56e14.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114357} {:answer/id #uuid "fd7b96c5-2ad9-5774-9aa1-adcd6b32e6aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/94/9457831d1de2697c57d827c12fe1919c35fa637e5d21621a949f04b88e9010dd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114358} {:answer/id #uuid "35b899f8-1a73-555a-aef4-38d360590a94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9c/9c045011d942bd93712aa87307994f00d9be9613c6dd547476f4fe7bd1622e19.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114359} {:answer/id #uuid "4c47f2ba-4f50-55b6-a56d-d0e4351c33ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f3/f3c81896babacce5e34f1cbb9f179f6843ae46fa45b8b4399b8f7f8eb11284c8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35b899f8-1a73-555a-aef4-38d360590a94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9c/9c045011d942bd93712aa87307994f00d9be9613c6dd547476f4fe7bd1622e19.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114359} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c778ab1-b212-513e-ba58-8b044eb94543" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114355}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "59f4234d-7f54-5341-b6b4-e5e2ca156720" :question/math-academy-id "q-55288" :question/problem "Which of the following number lines represents the values of $x$ that satisfy $2x\\le 8$ or $3x+4\\ge 7?$" :question/worked-solution "We start by solving $2x\\le 8:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & \\le 8 \\\\ x & \\le 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/f3/f3c81896babacce5e34f1cbb9f179f6843ae46fa45b8b4399b8f7f8eb11284c8.png)\n\nThen, we solve $3x+4\\ge 7:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+4 & \\ge 7 \\\\ 3x & \\ge 3 \\\\ x & \\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/c9/c9f85fc4864f321722a7cb0b017eab1979aa6a84cd07d08b150b625a1720f25a.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/9c/9c045011d942bd93712aa87307994f00d9be9613c6dd547476f4fe7bd1622e19.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $-\\infty <x<\\infty .$"}]}
